y 8 October will be introduced by art historian and Fashion in Film Festival director Marketa Uhlirova. A satirical, wild and irreverent story of rebellion, V&#283;ra Chytilov&#225;&#8217;s classic of surrealist cinema is perhaps also the most adventurous and anarchic Czech movie of the 1960s. Two young women,&hellip;\">\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://www.thegardencinema.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/films/Daisies.jpg\">\n<meta property=\"og:image:secure_url\" content=\"https://www.thegardencinema.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/films/Daisies.jpg\">\n<meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"559\">\n<meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"823\">\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary\">\n<meta name=\"twitter:site\" content=\"@thegardencinema\">\n<meta name=\"twitter:creator\" content=\"@thegardencinema\">\n<meta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"Daisies / The Garden Cinema\">\n<meta name=\"twitter:description\" content=\"Our screening on Thursday 8 October will be introduced by art historian and Fashion in Film Festival director Marketa Uhlirova. A satirical, wild and irreverent story of rebellion, V&#283;ra Chytilov&#225;&#8217;s classic of surrealist cinema is perhaps also the most adventurous and anarchic Czech movie of the 1960s. Two young women,&hellip;\">\n<meta name=\"twitter:image\" content=\"https://www.thegardencinema.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/films/Daisies.jpg\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"application/rss+xml\" title=\"The Garden Cinema &raquo; Feed\" href=\"https://www.thegardencinema.co.uk/feed/\" />\n<link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"application/rss+xml\" title=\"The Garden Cinema &raquo; Comments Feed\" href=\"https://www.thegardencinema.co.uk/comments/feed/\" />\n<link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"application/rss+xml\" title=\"The Garden Cinema &raquo; Daisies Comments Feed\" href=\"https://www.thegardencinema.co.uk/film/daisies/feed/\" />\n<script type=\"text/javascript\">\n/* <![CDATA[ */\nwindow._wpemojiSettings = {\"baseUrl\":\"htt